We have been able to keep exports to existing markets intact and, in addition, we have been successful in exporting to new markets.
Data from the One-Stop-Shop Secretariat for rice export formalities showed that Poland was the largest importer of rice at 27,764 tonnes, followed by France at 26,438 tonnes, Thailand at 22,250 tonnes, Malaysia at 20,095 tonnes and China at 13. 079 tons.
The same data shows that Amru Rice Cambodia was the leading exporter, exporting 22,399 tonnes, followed by Khmer Food with 21,704 tonnes and Golden Rice with 17,182 tonnes.
Cambodia's rice exports have continued to grow every year after the government set a policy of exporting 1 million tonnes in 2015.
An initiative by the European Union to help the least developed countries, that is, everything except arms, has enabled Cambodian rice to be exported duty-free to EU member states. Imports from Thailand and Vietnam are taxed at around 175 euros ($ 224) per tonne of rice.
