Cambodia's economic situation and progress
Cambodia's economy is on the right track to a strong recovery thanks to the efforts of the private sector and the government.
After suffering from the recession and the global financial crisis from 2009 to 2010, the GDP growth rate estimated by international financial institutions is recovering at a high level or may Say, perhaps one of the fastest growing economies in the region.
There are a number of key factors driving this growth, including exports, consumption and direct investment, especially diversified inflows on foreign direct investment (FDI).
In the ASEAN Development Outlook 2013, the ADB provides more details for its projections.
The company predicts that the industrial sector will grow by more than 10% in 2013 as EU demand for Cambodian products is steadily rising due to preferential market access under the European Initiative. All except weapons.
