Bicheng imports fall as Cambodia has packaging plant
Cambodia imported a total of 2,086 tonnes of packaged bicheng last year, the lowest level since 2002.
This is according to data imported from the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
As data on Bicheng imports dwindled, representatives of Bicheng Packaging, which has a factory in Cambodia, said demand for Bicheng was increasing year by year in line with population growth.
Thus, the drop in imports does not mean that Cambodians are turning away from the product, but the presence of local packaging plants through investment from Japan's Ajinomoto. Reduce Cambodia's imports of beech.
