The potential market in Cambodia is around 20,000 tonnes per year, with an average per capita consumption of about 1.6 kg per year.
Cambodia does not yet have a Bicheng processing plant, but due to rising trade prices combined with rising labor costs in neighboring Cambodia, Ajinomoto has decided to invest in Bicheng packaging. In Cambodia to reduce production costs and make it easier to sell for the local market in Cambodia.
After the company invested in the Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone in 2010, imports of Bicheng products began to decline sharply.
