Speaking at the closing ceremony of the 2012 Water Resources Working Meeting in January this year, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology Lim Kean Hor said that until now, the possibility of irrigation by Cambodia's irrigation system was possible. Irrigated a total of 1.4 million hectares, accounting for about 63 percent of Cambodia's total arable land.
However, Dr. Yang Saing Koma, President of CEDAC, one of the largest agricultural development organizations in Cambodia, said that there are a total of more than 2,000 irrigation systems in Cambodia, but there are only canals that can be used. Only about 10 percent.
