Phnom Penh: Aeon Microfinance Institution, part of AEON Group in Japan, said that sales of electronics and motorcycles through installments in the first quarter of this year increased by more than 700% compared to the same period last year Last year.
The trend, industry experts say, will increase further with growing demand for electronics.
Aeon Microfinance Institution Cambodia provides installment purchase services without providing direct loans to customers.
Customers can shop at electronics stores or motorcycle stores that have partnered with AEON and pay monthly installments to AEON at an interest rate of about 1.9% per month.
Aeon is currently one of the leading providers of this new product in Cambodia's narrow MFI market.
