Lack of transparency in the oil and gas sector
Cambodia's fledgling oil industry currently has very little government revenue due to a lack of transparency and vulnerability to corruption.
This is according to the report of the Revenue Monitoring Organization.
Cambodia ranks 52nd out of 58 countries on the Revenue Monitoring Institute's Resource Management Index, which scores lower on the level of transparency and separation of powers, but ranks higher on the legal framework.
This index measures the quality of management in the oil, gas and mining sectors.
