He said that after the completion of the new shopping center, he would gather all the vendors in the area into one place to avoid environmental pollution.
He also wants to seek help from the Ministry of Tourism to train local people who are responsible for serving tourists.
Khim Sanith, deputy director of the Koh Kong Provincial Department of Tourism, said that a resort can be stable for a long time only if it maintains good hygiene, good scenery, good cooperation from relevant institutions, especially good hospitality to guests.
