All car owners will be required to purchase insurance
All car owners in Cambodia will be required to purchase car insurance if the proposed amendments to the insurance law get the green light as the government seeks to bring the sector up to regional standards.
Currently, only commercial vehicles, such as buses, are required by law to purchase insurance.
However, the Ministry of Economy and Finance, which oversees the insurance industry, has suggested that private car owners who purchase insurance are liable to third parties who are damaged in the event of an accident.
