Exports to Japan up 23% in first three months
Cambodia's exports to Japan in the first three months of this year totaled $ 126 million, up 23 per cent from the same period last year.
According to trade data from the Japan External Trade Organization in Cambodia (JETRO), in the first quarter of 2012, Cambodia's exports to Japan totaled $ 102 million.
While the increase in exports from Cambodia to Japan is a positive sign in strengthening bilateral trade cooperation between the two countries, Japanese business representatives in Cambodia said that in addition to exports of garments and footwear, exports of manufactured goods Other effects are gaining momentum, with new developments showing that Cambodia's exports are beginning to diversify.
Kyoto Kadoho, JETRO's representative in Cambodia, told the Post that Cambodia's exports to Japan were in good shape and that Cambodia was now not only exporting garments, but also increasing its exports. Launch higher value-added products, such as electrical appliances installed by Japanese companies in Cambodia.
He added that more and more industrial plants were investing in Cambodia to assemble auto parts and export them back to Japan.
According to JETRO trade data, the main products that Cambodia exports to Japan are footwear, clothing and electrical machinery, and Cambodia also imports from Japan such as machinery for the car factory. Ships and boats.
