The inflow of foreign investment is steadily increasing, especially from Japanese investors, which clearly shows that Cambodia is a good investment destination.
Exports of Cambodian products to Japan have been gaining momentum, especially in recent years, as the flow of Japanese investment to Cambodia has become clearer through industrial projects.
In fact, in 2010, Cambodia exported a total of $ 209 million worth of its products to Japan, and the following year, exports increased to $ 309 million.
In 2012, Cambodia also exported a total of $ 404 million worth of products to Japan.
