Two-month tourists increase 17%
The number of international tourists visiting Cambodia in the first two months of this year increased by 17.5 per cent compared to the same period last year.
Statistics obtained by the Post from the Ministry of Tourism show that 789,866 international tourists visited Cambodia in the first two months of this year, compared with 672,127 in the same period last year.
Of all foreign tourists, 418,663 were air travelers, accounting for 53 per cent, while land and water tourists accounted for 371,203, accounting for 47 per cent of the total.
