He said the growth of visitors from the Asia-Pacific and ASEAN regions was still good and the European market was good.
Cambodia received more than 3.5 million international tourists in 2012, earning more than $ 2 billion.
Ministry requires tax agents to be licensed
The Ministry of Economy and Finance requires all tax service agents in Cambodia to have a license to guarantee the tax service profession.
This is according to the Prakas of the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
To date, all tax service providers in Cambodia have operated without a license.
Last month, the Ministry of Economy and Finance signed a prakas on the agency's licensing.
Following the full implementation of Prakas No. 455, signed on April 12, all agents must have a biennial license.
The taxpayer must be at least 18 years old, have a relevant degree or history of tax-related education for at least six months, and must have a letter of conviction.
Tax providers also have to pass an exam if they do not have a professional certification from the Ministry or the Institute of Public Accountants of Cambodia and the KICPAA or a former tax official.
This will be done in the next few months.
Operating without a license will require the agency to pay a fine of 10 million riel and likely suspend for six months, while taxpayers who use unlicensed agents will also be fined 5 million riel. .
Chan Sophal, president of the Cambodian Economic Association, said it was good to have a formal service for customers.
According to a Prakas of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, an individual tax agency will pay a license fee of 1 million riel to the General Department of Taxation, while a company agency must pay 2 million riel. Riel.
