Cambodia-Thailand bilateral trade down
Bilateral trade between Cambodia and Thailand fell slightly in the first quarter of this year compared to the same period last year.
Trade volume fell by about 2.5 percent to about $ 1.1 billion in the first quarter, according to trade data from the Thai Embassy in Phnom Penh.
A senior Thai embassy official said the border dispute did not affect the two countries' trade activities, but the decline in the competitiveness of Thai goods in the market. The appreciation of the baht against the dollar was the main reason for the decline.
