He said that according to the plan, the community plans to produce 80,000 tons of salt to meet the needs of the country, but this plan will face obstacles because of the heavy rains before the Khmer New Year, making the salt in the fields not collected. The result is all damaged.
However, the supply of salt next year will not be in short supply, as last year's salt surplus reached more than 100,000 tonnes, while the country's annual demand is around 8-10. Ten thousand tons.
Prime Minister Hun Sen said at the inauguration of the Kampot provincial hall yesterday that although salt production was almost 50 percent less than planned, the remaining amount Last year was large and could supply local demand without shortage and did not cause the price of salt to rise.
He also pointed out the two contradictory situations: if the dry season lasts too long, salt production will be more productive, but the dams in the province will be the same, with less water and more power shortages. Power supply.
