China has become the fifth largest importer of rice for the Cambodian rice market.
In January, the new port of the Phnom Penh Autonomous Port officially opened in response to the current surge in shipments.
The new port is located in Kandal province's Kien Svay district, about 30 kilometers from the Phnom Penh Autonomous Port, at a cost of more than $ 28 million under a Chinese government loan.
Phnom Penh Autonomous Port is another state-owned enterprise that plans to list on the Cambodian Stock Exchange.
