The Asian Development Bank (ADB) has forecast that Cambodia will grow 7.2 percent this year, up from 7.5 percent in 2014, due to the recovery of its major export partners, the United States and the United Kingdom. Europe.
The region as a whole is projected to grow at an average of about 5.75 percent this year due to rising external demand.
But the IMF's global economic outlook also warns that potential dangers inside and outside the region could jeopardize the hopeful scenario.
In the face of the global economic downturn, declining external demand will hurt the ASEAN economy.
