Data from the General Department of Taxation showed total tax revenue of $ 122.17 million.
Meanwhile, tax revenue from telecommunications rose 94.3 percent, beverage revenue rose 28.3 percent, education rose 1.39 percent, motor oil and gasoline rose 13.5 percent. Tariffs on imports and exports rose 17.4 percent Garments rose 41.8 percent Consumer taxes rose 26.8 percent Construction and engineering increased 159 percent Transport and tourism grew 34.2 percent, hotels and guesthouses rose 20.3 percent.
Kong Vibol, the newly appointed director general of the General Department of Taxation, said in a statement earlier this month that the increase in tax revenue reflects an increase in new business ventures, especially the efforts of Tax officials in an attempt to collect taxes.
He said the tax department would try to cooperate with commercial banks to make it easier for taxpayers and make tax collection more transparent.
