Confidence is the foundation of success
When he was a child living in the jungle in Kampong Thom province, his mother was sent to work all day in the fields during the Khmer Rouge regime.
Tith Hong Yoeu, even though he was only three years old, walked out of his palm-leaf hut into a forest lake to catch frogs, crabs and fish for grilling.
That experience made this Cambodian child more self-reliant than anyone else had ever been.
What seems sad is that a boy from dawn to dusk every day made up his own true success story in Cambodia.
Today, Dr. Tith serves as director of the Roomchang Department of Dentistry and Aesthetics, located in a 10-story building he designed directly along Street 184 at the corner of Norodom Street.
Dr. Tith said in an interview last week:
If you were born in a bad situation, it is because of society and the country as well as politics today.
When the country is peaceful and you are still in a bad situation, it makes no progress and you become a negative person.
Dr. Tit's advice for Cambodians to be successful is to look at the freedom they have to travel and do things.
A development environment where other countries do not exist, where people can have one idea one day and make it happen the next.
We have more freedom because the laws are not as strict as in developed countries.
This problem may not occur in Europe because there are not many restrictions.
And do not complain too much about the past.
The Prime Minister has also been open to this type of development from the private sector.
He said that the best teacher in his life gave a lot of ideas.
We have many ways to improve our lives through continuing education.
We can save money and spend more on education.
Tith said that in a capital-intensive system, you should not be happy with what you get empty-handed, but you should be happy when you spend what you want, you get what you need and Really want it.
